  "verbalization": "Prednisolone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Discoid Lupus Erythematosus through a mechanism involving the use of its metabolites or related compounds. The evidence suggests that Prednisolone, through its indication for Exanthem and Chronic Primary Adrenal Insufficiency, may indirectly influence the disease. Specifically, the pathway involving Desoximetasone and Methylprednisolone, both of which are indicated for Discoid Lupus Erythematosus, indicates a potential link between Prednisolone and the disease. The overlapping indications for Methylprednisolone in multiple paths suggest a possible role in the disease process, though the exact mechanism remains unclear. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible dependency on corticosteroids, which are known to have immunomodulatory effects, potentially contributing to the inflammatory and autoimmune features of Discoid Lupus Erythematosus.",
